rprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","02.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":234,"title":205,"body":235,"description":1201,"extension":1202,"links":1203,"meta":1204,"navigation":1205,"path":206,"seo":1206,"stem":207,"__hash__":1207},"docs\u002F02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format.md",{"type":236,"value":237,"toc":1184},"minimark",[238,242,246,250,261,268,272,282,288,292,297,300,339,343,350,357,363,367,374,429,439,452,516,519,587,590,594,597,603,607,610,616,620,623,629,633,640,880,884,890,1091,1095,1180],[239,240,25],"h2",{"id":241},"overview",[243,244,245],"p",{},"A CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier) is used by Kinotic to route requests to the appropriate service, method, or event stream. It is a URI-like format with parts named for clarity within the Kinotic platform.",[239,247,249],{"id":248},"format","Format",[251,252,257],"pre",{"className":253,"code":255,"language":256},[254],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@][zone~]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[258,259,255],"code",{"__ignoreMap":260},"",[243,262,263,264,267],{},"Everything in brackets (",[258,265,266],{},"[]",") is optional.",[239,269,271],{"id":270},"case","Case",[243,273,274,275,278,279,281],{},"Every part keeps the case it was written with, and addresses match by exact string comparison — ",[258,276,277],{},"OrderService"," and ",[258,280,277],{}," are two different addresses. Service names carry the case of the class that published them, so a typical address looks like:",[251,283,286],{"className":284,"code":285,"language":256},[254],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~org.kinotic.management.api.services.ProjectService\u002FfindByRepoFullName\n",[258,287,285],{"__ignoreMap":260},[239,289,291],{"id":290},"components","Components",[293,294,296],"h3",{"id":295},"scheme","Scheme",[243,298,299],{},"Identifies the type of resource being addressed.",[301,302,303,315],"table",{},[304,305,306],"thead",{},[307,308,309,312],"tr",{},[310,311,296],"th",{},[310,313,314],{},"Description",[316,317,318,329],"tbody",{},[307,319,320,326],{},[321,322,323],"td",{},[258,324,325],{},"srv",[321,327,328],{},"Published services and their methods",[307,330,331,336],{},[321,332,333],{},[258,334,335],{},"stream",[321,337,338],{},"Event streams (not yet routable through the gateway)",[293,340,342],{"id":341},"scope","Scope",[243,344,345,346,349],{},"An optional qualifier that narrows the CRI to a specific context, such as a tenant ID, user ID, or device ID. When present, it appears before the ",[258,347,348],{},"@"," symbol.",[243,351,352,353,356],{},"If a scope needs sub-scopes, use the format ",[258,354,355],{},"scope:sub-scope",".",[251,358,361],{"className":359,"code":360,"language":256},[254],"srv:\u002F\u002Ftenant-123@app.acme-org.orders-app~OrderService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fdevice-42@app.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[258,362,360],{"__ignoreMap":260},[293,364,366],{"id":365},"zone","Zone",[243,368,369,370,373],{},"The optional zone places the resource in the isolation boundary the gateway validates on every send and subscribe. It precedes the resourceName, separated by ",[258,371,372],{},"~",". A zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[301,375,376,384],{},[304,377,378],{},[307,379,380,382],{},[310,381,366],{},[310,383,314],{},[316,385,386,399,409,419],{},[307,387,388,393],{},[321,389,390],{},[258,391,392],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>",[321,394,395,396,356],{},"One application's services. Only that application's participants and the owning organization's runtimes can call them, through the app server, the one server that reaches these zones; they are hosted by the owning organization's runtime, which authenticates as an organization participant. Applications may nest their own sub-zones, e.g. ",[258,397,398],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app.billing",[307,400,401,406],{},[321,402,403],{},[258,404,405],{},"app-api",[321,407,408],{},"The platform's data plane for applications, such as entity persistence and named query execution. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[307,410,411,416],{},[321,412,413],{},[258,414,415],{},"management-api",[321,417,418],{},"The platform services organizations manage the system through, such as member, application, and entity definition management. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[307,420,421,426],{},[321,422,423],{},[258,424,425],{},"system-api",[321,427,428],{},"Platform-internal services. Only system participants can call or host them.",[243,430,431,432,435,436,438],{},"Organization and application ids become zone labels, but only ever after the ",[258,433,434],{},"app"," prefix, so they cannot collide with the platform's own zones. The one exception is guarded explicitly: creating an organization or application whose name slugifies to ",[258,437,425],{}," is rejected.",[243,440,441,442,444,445,448,449,451],{},"Which zones a connection may address is determined by the authenticated participant. A participant may also address any sub-zone of a zone it is allowed, so ",[258,443,398],{}," is reachable by whoever may reach ",[258,446,447],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app",". An address without a ",[258,450,372],{}," carries no zone at all and is only reachable by system participants.",[301,453,454,467],{},[304,455,456],{},[307,457,458,461,464],{},[310,459,460],{},"Participant",[310,462,463],{},"May send to",[310,465,466],{},"May subscribe to",[316,468,469,485,504],{},[307,470,471,474,482],{},[321,472,473],{},"APPLICATION (org, app)",[321,475,476,478,479],{},[258,477,405],{},", ",[258,480,481],{},"app.\u003Corg>.\u003Capp>",[321,483,484],{},"reply destinations only",[307,486,487,490,499],{},[321,488,489],{},"ORGANIZATION (org)",[321,491,492,478,494,478,496],{},[258,493,415],{},[258,495,405],{},[258,497,498],{},"app.\u003Corg>.*",[321,500,501,503],{},[258,502,498],{}," — its applications' zones",[307,505,506,509,512],{},[321,507,508],{},"SYSTEM",[321,510,511],{},"everything",[321,513,514],{},[258,515,425],{},[243,517,518],{},"Each server also has a zone partitioning, the zones it hosts and the zones it reaches. A node advertises a service\nto the cluster only in a zone its server hosts, and sends only to zones its server reaches: an address in any\nother zone has no handlers there. An address without a zone passes both.",[301,520,521,534],{},[304,522,523],{},[307,524,525,528,531],{},[310,526,527],{},"Server",[310,529,530],{},"Hosts",[310,532,533],{},"Reaches",[316,535,536,553,570],{},[307,537,538,541,545],{},[321,539,540],{},"org",[321,542,543],{},[258,544,415],{},[321,546,547,478,549,478,551],{},[258,548,415],{},[258,550,425],{},[258,552,405],{},[307,554,555,558,564],{},[321,556,557],{},"system",[321,559,560,478,562],{},[258,561,425],{},[258,563,415],{},[321,565,566,478,568],{},[258,567,425],{},[258,569,415],{},[307,571,572,574,581],{},[321,573,434],{},[321,575,576,478,578],{},[258,577,405],{},[258,579,580],{},"app.*",[321,582,583,478,585],{},[258,584,405],{},[258,586,580],{},[243,588,589],{},"The gateway applies the partitioning before a frame reaches the event bus: a send to a zone the server does not\nreach, or a subscription in a zone it does not host, is refused whatever the participant may address. The\nservice directory and listener monitors still see every registration in the cluster, so a service hosted by one\nserver shows as online from any other, while each server's MCP listing shows only the tools in zones it reaches.",[293,591,593],{"id":592},"resource-name","Resource Name",[243,595,596],{},"The name of the resource being addressed, excluding the zone. For services, this is the fully qualified service name. For streams, this is the event type name.",[251,598,601],{"className":599,"code":600,"language":256},[254],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\n",[258,602,600],{"__ignoreMap":260},[293,604,606],{"id":605},"path","Path"